  "observations": [
    "Image leaderboards still show a consistent answer-versus-grounding gap: choosing the right option is easier than grounding the right landmark.",
    "Video leaderboards show an even sharper semantic-versus-temporal gap, especially for Agent-State composite behavior recognition.",
    "Environment-aware reasoning is generally easier than Agent-State reasoning on images, but visibility localization still keeps the video side challenging.",
    "Cross-modality overlap is only moderate, which supports keeping both image and video halves of the benchmark instead of collapsing them into one table.",
    "Model-family trends differ by view: Qwen variants are broadly competitive, while some models spike on counting or recognition without matching localization quality."
  ]
